# Files the Makefile writes into the working tree and then moves elsewhere, or
# leaves behind for you to collect. None of them belong in the repository, and
# a failed `mv` is exactly when you would not notice one sitting there.
#
# `make dumpdata` writes a timestamped fixture here.
qatrack-dump-*.json
#
# `make supervisor-conf` renders these from deploy/supervisor/ before moving
# them into /etc/supervisor/conf.d. `make nginx-conf` does the same with
# qatrack.conf, which the /qatrack*.conf rule above already covers - these two
# were simply missed.
django-q2.conf
gunicorn.conf
# Screenshots captured when a Selenium test fails (see conftest.py)
selenium-screenshots/

# The distributed database schema diagram is a RELEASE artifact, not something
# a feature branch should carry. `poe schema` / `make schema` regenerate it,
# and without this a developer who runs either one - to look at the diagram,
# or because a task list told them to - ends up with it staged in an unrelated
# PR. The two historical diagrams (0.3.0, 3.1.0) and any already-committed one
# are tracked, and .gitignore does not apply to tracked files, so a release
# regeneration still shows up as a normal modification.
#
# Adding the diagram for a NEW minor line is deliberate: `git add -f`.
docs/developer/images/qatrack_schema_*.svg
